      "title": "Before You Start",
      "body": [
        "This is a 12-card taste of You Call Yourself A Friend. The real game is multiplayer: you pair up with someone, race to 25 points, and find out who actually pays attention.",
        "In the full game, one player is the subject each round. Their partner reads the card and locks in the answer they think is right. Everyone else in the room answers too. Whoever matches the subject's real answer scores.",
        "Here in the sample, you are alone with the cards. No partner. No score. Just you, browsing.",
        "Each card asks something about a person. Pick a specific friend in your head as you read. Look at the four options. Ask yourself: would they know my answer? Would I know theirs? Sit with the gap, if there is one.",
